"site-nav-button theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Site nav button
		<header>A site nav button shows or hides the side navigation of the page layout around it:  its icons only and back on a wide page, slid in and out on a narrow one.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a public `--ui-*` token on the element, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow
			root. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-site-nav-button" playground>
				<ui-page-layout style="min-height: 12em">
					<ui-app-menu slot="menu">
						<ui-site-nav-button slot="start"></>
						<ui-item slot="start">My site</>
					</>
					<ui-site-nav slot="drawer" appearance="nav" current="#home" pages="\[{ \"title\": \"Home\", \"href\": \"#home\", \"icon\": \"home\" }, { \"title\": \"Films\", \"href\": \"#films\", \"icon\": \"film\" }]"></>
					<ui-text paragraph>Press the button: the drawer shows only its icons, or all of it again.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
